+## Optimization applied (requests phase, 2026-10-06)
+
+### Changes (1 file, no factories, no app code, no other spec types)
+
+**`spec/rails_helper.rb`** only:
+
+1. `RequestNotifyEmailStub` module + `before(:suite)` prepend:
+   ```ruby
+   module RequestNotifyEmailStub
+     def send_email!
+       example = RSpec.current_example rescue nil
+       return true if example && example.metadata[:type] == :request && !example.metadata[:need_notification_email]
+       super
+     end
+   end
+   config.before(:suite) { NotifyService.prepend(RequestNotifyEmailStub) }
+   ```
+   Zero RSpec mock overhead, scoped via metadata, opt-out via `need_notification_email: true`.
+
+2. Webhook stub for requests (same as models):
+   ```ruby
+   config.before(:each, type: :request) do |example|
+     allow(TriggerWebhookWorker).to receive(:perform_async) unless example.metadata[:sidekiq_inline]
+   end
+   config.after(:each, type: :request) { Sidekiq::Worker.clear_all }
+   ```
+
+3. AR log silencing for requests (same as models):
+   ```ruby
+   config.around(:each, type: :request) do |example|
+     if example.metadata[:enable_logging]
+       example.run
+     else
+       orig = ActiveRecord::Base.logger; ActiveRecord::Base.logger = nil
+       begin; example.run; ensure; ActiveRecord::Base.logger = orig; end
+     end
+   end
+   ```
+
+4. `flushdb` extended to requests:
+   ```ruby
+   if [:model, :request].include?(example.metadata[:type])
+     redis.flushdb
+   else
+     redis.del(redis.keys)
+   end
+   ```
+
+### Why this is safe
+
+- Webhooks: no request spec asserts `TriggerWebhookWorker` via `have_enqueued` or `have_received` (only `admin/webhooks_spec` CRUD). Specs asserting other workers set `:fake` explicitly — unaffected. `inboxes_spec` local stub for `FollowersSynchronizationWorker` is different worker, compatible.
+- Notify emails: no request spec asserts `NotificationMailer` (`grep` none). `capture_emails` in requests only for `AdminMailer` (account_actions, reports) and empty-check (admin confirmations) — different paths, still pass (verified 0 failures). Service specs for `NotifyService` (type `:service`) still call `super` and pass (61 ex, 0 failures).
+- AR logging: no request spec asserts on SQL logs (`grep` none). `Rails.logger` left intact (same as models).
+- `flushdb` vs `del(keys)`: same effect on isolated test DB (DB 1, `redis.flushdb` in `after` + `Rails.cache.clear`). Other types (system, etc.) keep `del(keys)`.
+- `clear_all` after requests: no-op for inline tests, prevents fake-queue pollution for `:fake` tests (e.g., `to_not have_enqueued`).
+- Other spec types (`type != :request`, except models already optimized) keep exact previous behavior (`:inline`, `del(keys)`, logging, real Notify emails).
